#### Endcap Electromagnetic Calorimeter

Similar to the BEMC is the Endcap Electromagnetic Calorimeter, which extends STAR's calorimetry to include \(1<|\eta|<2\) and \(0<\phi<2\pi\). It is also used to measure energy of photons, electrons and positrons in the energy range \(0.2<E<150\;\mathrm{GeV}\). Like the BEMC, with which it shares many design features, the EEMC is a Shashlik type sampling calorimeter made of \(\mathrm{Pb}\) and plastic scintillator.

The EEMC consists of 720 towers of size \(\Delta\phi=0.1\) and ranging in \(0.057<\Delta\eta<0.099\), with \(\Delta\eta\) decreasing as \(\eta\) increases. These towers are arranged in rings of constant \(\eta\) as shown in Figure 4.13. In addition to towers, the EEMC features a Shower Maximum Detector as well

