shown in Figure 5.9a. Fits are done with the likelihood method using RooFit [155, 156]. The rest of the fits can be found in the Appendix B. The Figures 5.9b, 5.9c, 5.9d show mean \(\mu_{e}\), width \(\sigma_{e}\) and yield \(N_{e}\) respectively.

Finally, the efficiency is calculated with the Equation 5.4.

\[\epsilon=\frac{\int_{-1,2}^{3}f_{Gauss}(n\sigma_{e})dn\sigma_{e}}{\int_{- \infty}^{+\infty}f_{Gauss}(n\sigma_{e})dn\sigma_{e}} \tag{5.4}\]

The function \(f_{Gauss}\) above is the fitted Gaussian. The uncertainties are calculated using a binomial distribution [162]. A \(3\sigma\) uncertainty on the fit is included as a systematic uncertainty on the \(\Upsilon\) yield, which is described in Section 5.7.10. The resulting efficiency is used to calculate electron and \(\Upsilon\) reconstruction efficiency.

