because of larger yields in the data, which can be used to constrain the smearing parameter.. Figure 5.16a shows the comparison of \(J/\psi\) widths obtained from Crystal Ball fits to embedding and data. Figure 5.16b presents the dependence of \(\chi^{2}\) on \(a\) parameter. The best fit is found to be \(a=0.293^{+0.040}_{-0.045}\%\). The uncertainties on \(a\) are included in systematic uncertainty as described in Section 5.7.4.

