## Chapter 6 Data analysis for \(J/\psi\) production studies

The \(J/\psi\) analysis is done in a very similar way to the \(\Upsilon\) studies. Results of this analysis were published in Physical Review C [178].

### 6.1 Data set

The data set used for \(J/\psi\) analysis amounts to \(312\,{\rm M}\,p+p\) Min-Bias events recorded by STAR during 2009 (Run09) at \(\sqrt{s}=200\ {\rm GeV}\). These events had been registered with the use of VPD-MB trigger, which required a coincidence hits in both east and west VPD.

### 6.2 Event selection

The event selection is done first, by requiring \({\rm TriggerId}=240020,240025\) to accept only VPD-MB trigger events. Next, the reconstructed primary vertex \(V_{z}\) has to be within \(\pm 6\ {\rm cm}\) of the vertex position obtained from time difference between VPD hits \(V_{z}^{VPD}\) as defined by the cut \(\left|V_{z}-V_{z}^{VPD}\right|<6\ {\rm cm}\). This removes pile-up vertices and ensures, that the analyzed event is indeed the one, which fired the trigger. In addition, a good quality vertex is selected with \(rank(id=0)>0\) cut. Finally, to ensure a uniform acceptance and tracking efficiency the \(\left|V_{z}\right|<30\ {\rm cm}\) is applied.

