#### Additional smearing of electron \(p_{T}\)

Similarly to \(\varUpsilon\) analysis, the width of \(J/\psi\) lineshape is narrower in embedding than in the data. Additional Gaussian smearing is applied to electron \(p_{T}\), where the width of the Gaussian is \(\sigma=Ap_{T}\). The smeared lineshape is fitted to the signal in the data as can be seen for example in Figure 6.4b. This is done for different values of \(A\), so a \(\chi^{2}\) vs. \(A\) dependence is obtained. It is shown in Figure 6.15. The best fit is found for \(A=0.71\pm 0.05\).

