In order to reproduce a realistic \(J/\psi\)\(p_{T}\) and \(y\) spectra. The flat distribution in embedding is weighed with the function found in Equation 6.2.

\[w(p_{T},y)=f_{Gauss}(y,\mu=0,\sigma=1.416)\cdot Ap_{T}(1+(p_{T}/B)^{2})^{n} \tag{6.2}\]

The function was determined from a fit to STAR [180] and PHENIX [181]\(J/\psi\) data. The parameters are \(A=4.239\), \(B=3.699\,\mathrm{GeV/c}\), \(n=5\).

